{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/883", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Where is the quote \\\"frankly my dear, I don't give a damn\\\" from?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nIt's a famous quote from the movie Gone with the Wind.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nWhat is this movie about?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThe movie tells the story of the American Civil War and the Reconstruction era, through the life of a southern woman named Scarlett O'Hara. It's the highest-grossing film of all time, and is widely considered one of the greatest movies ever made.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nMake a poem about the story of gone with the wind\", \"response\": \"In the heart of the South, in a time of strife,\\n Lived Scarlett O'Hara, a girl full of life.\\n Belle of Tara, her plantation home,\\n Dreamed of wealth and power, her fate to roam.\\n \\n\\n But war came to Georgia, flames encroaching,\\n Leaving ash and ruin, the land dew-drenched.\\n Scarlett fought and persevered, love ever near,\\n Through loss and heartache, her fortitude clear.\\n \\n\\n After the war, desperation deep,\\n Scarlett vowed to save her ancestral keep.\\n Rhett Butler, the rogue she'd met,\\n A partner in her plans, their fates set.\\n \\n\\n With strength and determination, she reclaimed her land,\\n Bankrupting Yankees, ruthless and grand.\\n But Scarlett's love for Rhett, never secure,\\n Left their passionate bond, cracked and unsure.\\n \\n\\n Her heart belonged to one, who'd gone away,\\n To Ashley Wilkes, a lost cause of the gray.\\n Yet Rhett loved Scarlett, despite her flaws,\\n His final words to her, he left no pause:\\n \\n\\n \\\"Frankly, my dear, I don't give a damn,\\\"\\n He left her love, on that sorrowful span.\\n Scarlett was left with the fire inside,\\n To build her empire, never to be denied.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/91", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"i want you to act as an expert chrome extension developer. i want to create a brief for my upwork job. the job is to create a very simple chrome extension that lets users access our eli5 feature that takes a prompt and sends it to davinci 003 via api and returns a completion. write a brief for me\", \"response\": \"To create a simple Chrome extension that allows users to access your ELI5 (Explain Like I'm 5) feature, you will need to follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Define the purpose and goals of the extension:\\n\\n- The extension should allow users to access the ELI5 feature from within the Chrome browser.\\n- The extension should be easy to use and should provide a seamless experience for users.\\n\\n2. Determine the functionality of the extension:\\n\\n- The extension should have a simple user interface that allows users to enter a prompt or question.\\n- The extension should send the prompt to the Davinci 003 API and receive a completion in return.\\n- The extension should display the completion to the user in an easy-to-read format.\\n\\n3. Decide on the design of the extension:\\n\\n- The extension should have a clean and simple design that is easy to use and navigate.\\n- The extension should have a consistent look and feel with your brand.\\n\\n4. Plan the development of the extension:\\n\\n- The extension should be developed using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.\\n- The extension should use the Chrome API to interact with the browser.\\n- The extension should use the Davinci 003 API to send and receive data.\\n\\n5. Test and debug the extension:\\n\\n- The extension should be thoroughly tested to ensure that it works correctly on all supported versions of Chrome.\\n- The extension should be debugged to resolve any issues that may arise.\\n\\n6. Publish the extension on the Chrome Web Store:\\n\\n- The extension should be published on the Chrome Web Store for users to download and install.\\n- The extension should be regularly updated to ensure that it works correctly and is compatible with the latest versions of Chrome.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can create a simple Chrome extension that allows users to access your ELI5 feature from within the browser. The extension should be easy to use, functional, and provide a seamless experience for users.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/433", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Computing time deposit interest: why is the earnings of 100,000.00 principal only 215.28 from a 3.125% interest?\", \"response\": \"The interest rate of 3.125% is given as an annual rate. To calculate the interest earned over a period shorter than one year, we need to convert the interest rate to a periodic rate. The most common periodic rates are monthly, semi-annually, and quarterly. Let's assume the interest is compounded quarterly.\\n\\nThe quarterly interest rate is 3.125% / 4 = 0.78125%\\nThe interest earned in one quarter is 100,000.00 * 0.78125% = 781.25\\nThe interest earned in two quarters is 781.25 * 2 = 1562.50\\nThe interest earned in three quarters is 1562.50 * 3 = 4687.50\\nThe interest earned in one year is 4687.50 * 4 = 18750.00\\n\\nSo the interest earned on the principal of 100,000.00 with a 3.125% interest rate compounded quarterly for one year is 18750.00.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/1035", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"The seven deadly sins, also known as the seven cardinal vices, are a group of behaviors traditionally viewed as being unhealthy or harmful to society. These sins are typically listed as pride, greed, lust, envy, wrath, sloth, and gluttony.\\n \\n\\n It's important to recognize that these concepts are cultural\\n and historical constructs. It's natural for all humans to\\n experience a range of desires and emotions, including those\\n that are sometimes labeled as \\\"sins.\\\" \\n \\n\\n Understanding human urges and emotions from a place\\n of nonjudgment can be an excellent way to gain insight \\n into the human experience.\\n Yes, the seven deadly sins are a cultural and historical construct, and it's important to understand that what may be considered a sin or vice in one culture or society may not be viewed the same way in another. Additionally, it's important to recognize that experiencing a range of emotions and desires is a normal part of the human experience, and to approach them with nonjudgment and an understanding of how they can offer insight into the human experience.\\n \\n\\n \\n\\n \\n\\n \\n\\n Raina D\\n Do you know about the 12 archetypes?\\n Yes, the 12 archetypes is a concept developed by Carl Jung, a Swiss psychiatrist and psychoanalyst, in his work on personality theory. Jung believed that the psyche is made up of various archetypes, which are universal patterns or themes that are present in the collective unconscious of all human beings. The 12 archetypes he identified include the Innocent, the Orphan, the Hero, the Caregiver, the Explorer, the Rebel, the Lover, the Jester, the Sage, the Magician, the Regular Guy/Girl, and the Teacher. Jung believed that each individual has a dominant archetype that shapes their personality and behavior, but that all of the archetypes are present in the psyche to some degree.\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThank you for your question. You are correct that the 12 archetypes are a core component of Jungian psychology, and are sometimes referred to as \\\"universal patterns of the psyche.\\\" Jung believed that these archetypes are present in the collective unconscious of all human beings, and that they shape our personality and behavior in various ways.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nPlease connect 3 sins/vices to each of the archetypes. Like if the vices were seen as human urges which archetypes would be more like to be affected by which vices?\", \"response\": \"Here is a table connecting the seven deadly sins/cardinal vices to the 12 archetypes:\\n \\n\\n Deadly Sin/Cardinal Vice Archetype(s)\\n Pride Innocent, Hero, Regular Guy/Girl\\n Greed Orphan, Regular Guy/Girl\\n Lust Lover, Jester, Rebel\\n Envy Orphan, Teacher, Sage\\n Wrath Hero, Rebel, Teacher\\n Sloth Innocent, Orphan, Jester\\n Gluttony Lover, Jester, Rebel\\n \\n\\n Note: The connection between the archetypes and the deadly sins/cardinal vices is not a one-to-one correspondence, as each archetype can be affected by multiple vices and each vice can affect multiple archetypes. The table above is meant to provide a general guide for how the vices may relate to certain archetypes.\\n \\n\\n Here are some additional insights into how each archetype may be affected by the seven deadly sins/cardinal vices:\\n \\n\\n 1. Pride: The Innocent and Hero archetypes may be prone to pride, as they often have a strong sense of their own worth and value. The Regular Guy/Girl archetype may also be susceptible to pride, as they may feel that they are better than others due to their status or accomplishments.\\n \\n\\n 2. Greed: The Orphan archetype may be prone to greed, as they may feel a lack of security and seek to accumulate wealth and resources to feel safe. The Regular Guy/Girl archetype may also be susceptible to greed, as they may prioritize material success and accumulation over other values.\\n \\n\\n 3. Lust: The Lover archetype may be prone to lust, as they are focused on physical and emotional pleasure. The Jester and Rebel archetypes may also be susceptible to lust, as they may seek to break free from societal norms and restrictions.\\n \\n\\n 4. Envy: The Orphan and Teacher archetypes may be prone to envy, as they may feel a sense of lack or inadequacy that leads them to desire what others have. The Sage archetype may also be susceptible to envy, as they may feel a sense of superiority to others and desire recognition and validation.\\n \\n\\n 5. Wrath: The Hero and Rebel archetypes may be prone to wrath, as they may feel a strong sense of justice and be quick to anger when they feel that their values or beliefs are being threatened. The Teacher archetype may also be susceptible to wrath, as they may feel a sense of responsibility to correct others' mistakes and hold them accountable.\\n \\n\\n 6. Sloth: The Innocent and Jester archetypes may be prone to sloth, as they may lack motivation and be content to live in the moment without thinking about the future. The Orphan archetype may also be susceptible to sloth, as they may feel overwhelmed and lack the energy to take action.\\n \\n\\n 7. Gluttony: The Lover and Rebel archetypes may be prone to gluttony, as they may seek out physical pleasure and indulge in excess. The Jester archetype may also be susceptible to gluttony, as they may use food and other forms of pleasure to cope with stress and anxiety.\\n \\n\\n It's important to remember that these are generalizations and that each individual's personality and behavior is complex and multifaceted. The connection between the seven deadly sins/cardinal vices and the 12 archetypes can be a helpful tool for understanding how our personality and behavior may be affected by these universal patterns, but it's not a definitive or exhaustive list.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/832", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Provide a list of 15 postpartum recovery tips for new mothers. Give recovery tips in bulleted points. It should be lighthearted, and each tip given should be briefly explained.\", \"response\": \"Postpartum recovery can be challenging for new mothers as they adjust to a new role and lifestyle. Mothers need to take care of themselves both physically and emotionally as their emotions and hormones recover:\\n\\n* **Nap When Baby Naps**: Seize quiet moments for a snooze. It's like a stealth mission for rest.\\n* **Stay Hydrated**: Always have a water bottle nearby. It's like your new best friend, but less chatty.\\n* **Snack Smart**: Keep nutritious snacks within reach. You're a snack ninja now.\\n* **Say 'Yes' to Help**: When offered help, take it. It's like having sidekicks in your superhero journey.\\n* **Comfort is Queen**: Embrace soft, stretchy clothing. Your wardrobe is now a hug in fabric form.\\n* **Gentle Movement**: Start with light walks. Think of it as a leisurely parade celebrating you.\\n* **Sitz Bath Bliss**: Soothe yourself with a sitz bath. It's spa time for your sore bits.\\n* **Laugh a Lot**: Indulge in your favorite comedy. Laughter is great, but maybe don't split your sides.\\n* **Befriend Fiber**: Keep your diet fiber-rich to stay regular. It’s less glamorous but super important.\\n* **Mindful Moments**: Try meditation or gentle yoga. It's like a serene vacation for your mind.\\n* **Skin Care Routine**: Pamper your skin with a gentle moisturizer or products designed for postpartum care. Ingredients like cocoa butter or vitamin E can be soothing for stretch marks or itchy skin. Think of it as nourishing your skin's storybook of motherhood.\\n* **Journal Your Journey**: Write about your experiences. Future you will appreciate these memoirs.\\n* **Professional Support**: If you're feeling overwhelmed, consider reaching out to a therapist, postpartum doula, or a support group for new mothers. They are like navigators in the sea of postpartum emotions, helping you find your bearings.\\n* **Love Your Body**: It did something amazing. Celebrate it in all its glory and patience.\\n* **Celebrate Small Wins**: Whether it's a shower or a walk around the block, it's a victory.\\n\\nRemember, this is a special time, and taking care of yourself is as important as taking care of your baby. Enjoy the journey!\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/628", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"focus on 2nd Place Is Just The 1st Loser 🥈 in a career search,  with an email to my tribe, and the CTA of a discovery call\", \"response\": \"Subject: Don't settle for 2nd place in your career search 🥈 Book a discovery call with me today!\\n\\nDear [Tribe’s Name],\\n\\nI hope this email finds you all well and thriving in your careers! As a member of our [tribe's name] community, I wanted to share some insights that I've gained through my own professional journey, which I believe could help some of you who might be seeking new opportunities or feeling stuck in your current roles.\\n\\nIn today's fast-paced and constantly evolving job market, it's easy to feel like you're constantly playing catch-up. The truth is, there will always be someone who seems to be more experienced, more connected, or more successful than you. However, that doesn't mean you should settle for being second best.\\n\\n\\\"Second place is just the first loser\\\" might sound harsh, but it's a mindset that I've adopted in my career, and it has helped me push myself beyond my comfort zone and achieve things I never thought were possible. The fact is, settling for second place means you're accepting a lower standard for yourself, and you're not giving yourself the chance to truly shine.\\n\\nThat's why I'm inviting you to book a discovery call with me today. During this call, we can discuss your career goals, identify any obstacles or challenges that you might be facing, and explore potential solutions that will help you rise above the competition.\\n\\nHere's what you can expect from our call:\\n\\n* A personalized and confidential conversation\\n* An opportunity to share your career goals and aspirations\\n* An analysis of your current skills, strengths, and areas for improvement\\n* Actionable advice and strategies that you can implement right away\\n* A roadmap for achieving your long-term career objectives\\n\\nI'm passionate about helping members of our community unlock their full potential, and I truly believe that everyone has what it takes to succeed in their careers. By investing just 30 minutes of your time, you could take a significant step towards reaching your career goals and leaving second place behind.\\n\\nTo book a discovery call, simply click on the link below and choose a time that works best for you. I can't wait to connect and help you take your career to the next level!\\n\\nBest regards,\\n\\n[Your Name]\\n\\n[Call to Action Button: Book a Discovery Call]\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
